<https://w3id.org/oc/meta/br/06260695455> a fabio:ScholarlyWork,
        fabio:Work ;
    dcterms:abstract "Data descriptor ; AbstractPrimary forests, defined here as forests where the signs of human impacts, if any, are strongly blurred due to decades without forest management, are scarce in Europe and continue to disappear. Despite these losses, we know little about where these forests occur. Here, we present a comprehensive geodatabase and map of Europe’s known primary forests. Our geodatabase harmonizes 48 different, mostly field-based datasets of primary forests, and contains 18,411 individual patches (41.1 Mha) spread across 33 countries. When available, we provide information on each patch (name, location, naturalness, extent and dominant tree species) and the surrounding landscape (biogeographical regions, protection status, potential natural vegetation, current forest extent). Using Landsat satellite-image time series (1985–2018) we checked each patch for possible disturbance events since primary forests were identified, resulting in 94% of patches free of significant disturbances in the last 30 years. Although knowledge gaps remain, ours is the most comprehensive dataset on primary forests in Europe, and will be useful for ecological studies, and conservation planning to safeguard these unique forests. ; Frankfurt Zoological Society (FZS; project ETN-WIE-FZS-001) ; European Commission (Marie Sklodowska‐Curie fellowship to FMS, project FORESTS & CO, #658876) ; Department for Nature Protection of the Italian Ministry of the Environment, Land and Sea Protection ; The GEVFP’s French dataset was supported by funding from EU, RF and ‘Conseil Régional Midi-Pyrénées’ ; Czech Science Foundation (Grant GACR no. 21-27454S), as well as the institutional project EVA No.CZ.02.1.01/ 0.0/0.0/16_019/0000803 ; Ministry of Education, Science and Technological Development of the Republic of Serbia, grant number 451-03-9/2021-14/ 200197 ; Funding programme Open Access Publishing by the German Research Foundation (DFG) ; Open Access funding enabled and organized by Projekt DEAL"@en ;
    dcterms:title "European Primary Forest Database V2.0",
        "European primary forest database v2.0 ; European primary forest database (EPFD) v2.0"@en ;
